From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amaan Qureshi <git@amaanq.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 06:12:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] geolocation: use the page URL as the TWA scope for delegation

InstalledWebappGeolocationBridge handed androidx the bare origin, but
TrustedWebActivityServiceConnectionPool.createServiceIntent() resolves the
owning client package by querying VIEW activities for that URI, so an origin
can never match a TWA whose intent filter is path scoped. Maps Go registers
/maps, so every delegated request died in createServiceIntent with
IllegalArgumentException("No service exists for scope") before any bind, which
is why tiles rendered while the location dot never appeared. The sibling path
in LocationPermissionUpdater already passes lastCommitedUrl for this reason.
GetTwaScopeUrl() prefers the WebContents last committed URL and falls back to
the origin unless it is same origin, leaving origin_ to keep driving permission
revocation.
